# LUKS2 data-disk encryption keyfile (encryption at rest).
#
# This .example is a PLACEHOLDER. The real keyfile is the unlock secret for the
# node's encrypted data partition (/mnt/data, which backs the cluster PVCs +
# relocated containerd/kubelet/Vault state) and MUST NEVER be committed — custody
# is this offline USB-KEYS stick (and Vault), the same model as the cluster CA
# and the Vault seal keys.
#
# Generate a strong random keyfile and drop it next to this file as
#   secrets/luks.key   (gitignored)
# e.g.:
#   head -c 64 /dev/urandom > secrets/luks.key && chmod 0600 secrets/luks.key
#
# keys-provision (provision_storage) uses it to luksFormat/open each device whose
# provision.json storage entry has encrypt:true (the default). On x86 / TPM nodes
# it ALSO enrolls TPM2 auto-unlock, leaving this keyfile as the recovery slot; on
# a Pi5 (no TPM) this keyfile is the only unlock path. Point a different path via
# provision.json .storage.luks_keyfile. See docs/ENCRYPTION-AT-REST.md.
